# DevOps Conventions

## Makefile is the Single Entry Point

ALL operations go through the Makefile. Never run raw `gcloud`, `pulumi`, or `firebase` commands.

Key targets:

| Target             | Description                                  |
|--------------------|----------------------------------------------|
| `make env-staging` | Switch to staging environment                |
| `make env-prod`    | Switch to prod (requires confirmation)       |
| `make preview`     | Pulumi preview (dry run)                     |
| `make deploy-infra`| Deploy infrastructure via Pulumi             |
| `make deploy-frontend` | Build and deploy frontend to Firebase    |
| `make deploy-all`  | Deploy infra then frontend, in order         |
| `make health`      | Run post-deploy health checks (12 checks)    |
| `make seed-firestore` | Seed test data into Firestore             |

## Pulumi Backend

Uses a shared GCS bucket backend configured in `scripts/_common.sh`:

```bash
export PULUMI_BACKEND_URL="${PULUMI_BACKEND_URL:-gs://kalilos-connector-pulumi-state}"
export PULUMI_CONFIG_PASSPHRASE="${PULUMI_CONFIG_PASSPHRASE:-}"
```

State lives in `gs://kalilos-connector-pulumi-state` (versioned), shared by local and CI deploys. No Pulumi Cloud account needed. The bucket and one-time state migration are handled by `scripts/bootstrap-cicd.sh`.

## GCP Account Guard

Every deployment script sources `scripts/_common.sh` which verifies the active GCP account is `nivbraz90@gmail.com`. If the check fails, the script aborts with instructions to re-authenticate. The Makefile `check-auth` target is a prerequisite of all deploy/preview/destroy targets.

In CI (GitHub Actions sets `CI=true`), the account guard is skipped — auth comes from Workload Identity Federation via Application Default Credentials, not the local gcloud named configuration.

## Shell Scripts

All scripts in `scripts/` must source `_common.sh` instead of defining their own `log`/`error`/`set -euo pipefail`:

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
source "$SCRIPT_DIR/_common.sh"
check_gcp_account
```

`_common.sh` provides: `set -euo pipefail`, `log()`, `error()`, `check_gcp_account()`, and Pulumi backend env vars.

## Environment Management

- `.env.staging` and `.env.prod` contain project-specific vars (git-ignored)
- `.env.example` is the committed template
- `make env-staging` loads staging config and sets Pulumi stack to `staging`
- `make env-prod` loads prod config, sets stack to `prod`, and prompts for confirmation

## Deployment Checklist

1. `make env-{target}` — set environment
2. `make preview` — review changes (REQUIRED before destructive ops)
3. `make deploy-all` — apply changes
4. `make health` — verify deployment (all 12 checks should pass)
